cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this plugin in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "research-co-pilot: a Claude co-pilot for the entire research lifecycle"
abstract: >
  research-co-pilot is a Claude Code and claude.ai plugin for academic and applied research.
  It bundles 14 skills covering the research lifecycle — literature review, methodology design
  (with mandatory creative AI / ML / Big Data extensions), ethics committee stress-testing,
  data analysis, qualitative coding, brainstorming, manuscript drafting (with voice preservation
  and academic-register enforcement), replication design, grant writing, talk building,
  reviewer-response drafting, citation formatting, survey design, and peer review (with anchored
  annotations across DOCX / PDF / PPTX / LaTeX) — alongside subagents for parallel source-reading,
  heavy data analysis, transcript coding, manuscript drafting, and independent stats validation.
  Designed to refuse common AI failure modes (fabricated citations, p-hacking, themes-without-an-audit-trail,
  averaging away disagreement in the literature) and to support multiple languages including Hebrew.
